WEBVTT

00:04.760 --> 00:09.600
<b><i>So, even with the One-Shot Kill, 
we couldn't defeat Miss Hundred Faces.</i></b>

00:10.080 --> 00:12.700
<b><i>Yeah, I should've expected that.</i></b>

00:12.700 --> 00:14.680
<b>Kind of a bad situation, huh?</b>

00:14.680 --> 00:15.110
<b>Oh?</b>

00:16.950 --> 00:18.200
<b>Saionji?</b>

00:23.820 --> 00:27.700
<b>Huh. And here I was thinking 
you'd be kind of down.</b>

00:27.700 --> 00:29.590
<b>Speak for yourself.</b>

00:29.590 --> 00:32.250
<b>Ahem. Guess you're right. But so what?</b>

00:34.780 --> 00:39.050
<b>Saionji, I called you here because 
I have something important to say.</b>

00:39.050 --> 00:41.930
<b>Huh? To me personally, Shinohara?</b>

00:41.930 --> 00:43.050
<b>Saionji...</b>

00:43.050 --> 00:46.010
<b>W-Wait, wait! My heart isn't ready for this!</b>

00:46.610 --> 00:49.030
<b>Would you hide up there for a bit?</b>

00:49.410 --> 00:50.290
<b>Say what?</b>

00:52.530 --> 00:57.530
<b>Together with You</b>

00:55.010 --> 00:58.120
<b>As you know, our attempt 
at all-out war was a bust.</b>

00:58.960 --> 01:01.370
<b>Basically, we can't beat Miss Hundred Faces...</b>

01:01.370 --> 01:04.210
<b>or rather, Shiina Tsumugi 
head-on. It's impossible.</b>

01:05.060 --> 01:07.540
<b>So are we just, like, giving up?</b>

01:07.540 --> 01:12.050
<b>Nope, no way. If the enemy's gonna 
do whatever it takes, so will we.</b>

01:12.050 --> 01:14.280
<b>We shall fight with all we have.</b>

01:14.280 --> 01:16.800
<b>You say that, but there's
a huge gulf in firepower.</b>

01:17.380 --> 01:19.510
<b>It won't be easy to turn it around.</b>

01:19.510 --> 01:23.500
<b>So we bring the fight to her by
setting up another game inside ASTRAL.</b>

01:23.500 --> 01:25.270
<b>One final game.</b>

01:26.860 --> 01:30.340
<b>This is something you've been planning, huh? 
You sure don't miss a step.</b>

01:30.340 --> 01:32.520
<b>But how do we convince her to participate?</b>

01:32.770 --> 01:37.020
<b>Good point. Miss Hundred Faces 
has already captured the most spaces.</b>

01:37.270 --> 01:41.310
<b>If she can win by just waiting it out, 
why would she bother with another game?</b>

01:41.310 --> 01:45.540
<b>Also, tomorrow's the final day. 
Kurahashi will definitely try to interfere.</b>

01:45.540 --> 01:48.250
<b>Yeah. With cheats and disruptions.</b>

01:48.250 --> 01:52.400
<b>All things considered, we will have 
to beat both Shiina and Kurahashi.</b>

01:53.140 --> 01:56.290
<b>Given all of that, do you still trust me?</b>

01:56.700 --> 01:57.390
<b>Yes.</b>

01:57.390 --> 01:58.470
<b>Of course we do!</b>

01:58.470 --> 01:59.330
<b>Sure.</b>

01:59.830 --> 02:00.800
<b>Guess I have to.</b>

02:03.580 --> 02:05.170
<b>I'm counting on you guys.</b>

02:05.460 --> 02:09.180
<b>Let's show them how strong we <i>really</i> are.</b>

02:09.560 --> 02:10.670
<b>All right!</b>

02:14.300 --> 02:17.610
<b>Now, how do I rope Shiina into another game?</b>

02:17.610 --> 02:19.620
<b>Ah, I was looking for you!</b>

02:20.040 --> 02:21.490
<b>Bro-bro!</b>

02:21.490 --> 02:23.150
<b><i>Is she planning something?</i></b>

02:24.620 --> 02:27.650
<b>Hey, let's go play some games!</b>

02:27.650 --> 02:28.370
<b>Huh?</b>

02:30.380 --> 02:33.310
<b>Aw, I lost again!</b>

02:32.400 --> 02:35.490
<b><i>She's acting like nothing's 
changed since yesterday.</i></b>

02:35.870 --> 02:39.370
<b>Hey. You really are Miss 
Hundred Faces, aren't you?</b>

02:39.630 --> 02:44.400
<b>Huh? Yeah, I am. I'm participating as 
a member of Seijo Academy. That's me!</b>

02:44.670 --> 02:47.390
<b>How did you get involved in all this, anyway?</b>

02:47.390 --> 02:49.080
<b>Huh? How?</b>

02:52.000 --> 02:58.610
<b>I don't really like school, so I always just stay 
home and play games and do computer stuff.</b>

02:58.610 --> 03:00.860
<b>Yeah, you said that before.</b>

03:00.860 --> 03:05.140
<b>I got into middle school and thought 
I'd be done with mandatory education soon</b>

03:05.140 --> 03:08.810
<b>and I wouldn't have to 
go to school anymore,</b>

03:08.810 --> 03:13.370
<b>but I realized if I don't get into high school, 
I can't play the star-catching game!</b>

03:13.370 --> 03:15.590
<b>Oh, yeah, I guess you're right.</b>

03:15.590 --> 03:19.380
<b>I didn't want to miss out 
on the star-catching game,</b>

03:19.380 --> 03:24.380
<b>so I modded my Device a little 
and force-installed a special program!</b>

03:24.380 --> 03:28.720
<b><i>That's all it took to make the first fake 
account in Academy Island history?</i></b>

03:29.290 --> 03:30.210
<b>Impressed?</b>

03:30.210 --> 03:32.730
<b>Y-Yeah, super impressed.</b>

03:35.170 --> 03:39.820
<b>And then, one day, I got a message 
from this person called Mikado something.</b>

03:41.060 --> 03:46.070
<b>He said, "I want you to join me," and,
"My group could use your talents," and stuff.</b>

03:46.070 --> 03:51.630
<b>It was <i>so</i> fishy! I mean, it sounded like
 some evil organization or something.</b>

03:51.630 --> 03:54.170
<b>So that's who invited me to ASTRAL.</b>

03:54.170 --> 03:58.030
<b>And he gave me a star that lets me
 make perfect copies of things.</b>

03:58.390 --> 04:02.060
<b>In exchange, he asked me to 
send that declaration of war.</b>

04:02.370 --> 04:06.300
<b>The one where I said I was gonna 
defeat you and the Empress, you know?</b>

04:06.300 --> 04:07.660
<b>Is that right?</b>

04:07.660 --> 04:09.420
<b><i>So that's what happened.</i></b>

04:12.200 --> 04:15.310
<b>Tomorrow's gonna be
 the final battle, right?</b>

04:15.870 --> 04:18.830
<b>The last day I get to play
 with you at the event.</b>

04:19.120 --> 04:24.810
<b>I'm so excited, I can't sleep at all...</b>

04:25.110 --> 04:26.900
<b><i>You just fell asleep.</i></b>

04:27.720 --> 04:32.770
<b><i>I guess Shiina hasn't been told 
anything about me and Saionji,</i></b>

04:32.770 --> 04:34.580
<b><i>and is just playing along.</i></b>

04:35.620 --> 04:41.660
<b><i>In ASTRAL, she'll be happy if she wins 
and sad if she loses. It's just a game to her.</i></b>

04:43.280 --> 04:48.470
<b><i>But she won't give up. She'll keep 
playing the game until somebody wins.</i></b>

04:48.960 --> 04:51.880
<b><i>So I have to convince her 
that she's already lost.</i></b>

04:51.880 --> 04:55.150
<b><i>I have to make her think the game is over.</i></b>

05:03.570 --> 05:08.660
<b>ASTRAL Final Day</b>

05:05.520 --> 05:10.200
<b><i>And so, we finally got the three 
surviving ASTRAL players together.</i></b>

05:11.770 --> 05:14.120
<b>Y-You know, Shiina...</b>

05:15.930 --> 05:18.290
<b>I'm Miss Hundred Faces right now.</b>

05:18.830 --> 05:21.300
<b>Could you change back to normal?</b>

05:21.300 --> 05:24.080
<b>Wouldn't that make it easier to show off?</b>

05:24.080 --> 05:25.150
<b>I guess you're right.</b>

05:25.520 --> 05:27.900
<b>Okay, if you insist.</b>

05:29.170 --> 05:31.010
<b>How's this, bro-bro?</b>

05:31.010 --> 05:32.530
<b>"Bro-bro"?</b>

05:32.530 --> 05:33.510
<b><i>Oh, crap!</i></b>

05:33.800 --> 05:37.770
<b>While we're at it, Shiina, this is the first time
 we're facing each other on the field,</b>

05:37.770 --> 05:40.230
<b>so can we review what's going on?</b>

05:40.230 --> 05:40.910
<b>Huh?</b>

05:41.330 --> 05:44.520
<b>There are only three academies
that haven't been eliminated.</b>

05:45.320 --> 05:48.020
<b>Ouka, Eimei, and Seijo.</b>

05:48.020 --> 05:53.980
<b>And I have the most area captured, the 
most spells, and the highest support rating!</b>

05:53.980 --> 05:57.100
<b>You sure do. But aren't you 
forgetting something, Shiina?</b>

05:57.100 --> 05:57.950
<b>Huh?</b>

05:57.950 --> 06:01.970
<b>Before this event started, 
you picked a fight with Saionji, right?</b>

06:02.580 --> 06:05.930
<b>You boldly declared war on her on ITube.</b>

06:07.710 --> 06:10.410
<b>Oh, uh, yeah. I guess I did.</b>

06:10.410 --> 06:14.120
<b>Remember the main rule of the 
game you challenged Saionji to?</b>

06:14.120 --> 06:15.920
<b>You haven't forgotten, have you?</b>

06:15.920 --> 06:19.060
<b>I said whoever beats you is the winner.</b>

06:19.060 --> 06:24.570
<b>That's right. So, basically, our ranks 
in ASTRAL don't really matter.</b>

06:25.580 --> 06:30.080
<b>I think you said something else, too. 
That if neither of you can beat me,</b>

06:30.080 --> 06:33.500
<b>then I'd be considered the 
victor of the Empress battle.</b>

06:34.370 --> 06:38.440
<b>And I'd get to decide what 
happens to you. Remember?</b>

06:38.440 --> 06:41.500
<b>Huh? Did I really say that?</b>

06:41.500 --> 06:44.030
<b>Uh, I guess I might have.</b>

06:44.030 --> 06:49.480
<b>That means, in the battle over the title of 
"Empress," I could win just by running away.</b>

06:49.910 --> 06:53.060
<b>In other words, there's no reason 
for me to fight you at all.</b>

06:53.060 --> 06:58.480
<b>But if I did that, it would mean 
I lose ASTRAL. Same goes for Saionji.</b>

06:58.960 --> 07:02.030
<b>I'm not losing the 
Empress's throne to you, kid.</b>

07:02.030 --> 07:07.060
<b>So I'd be totally fine with 
Shinohara running away. But...</b>

07:07.360 --> 07:14.570
<b>If you do win ASTRAL, then Ouka drops to 
at least sixth place, and I can't accept that.</b>

07:14.570 --> 07:20.080
<b>So because of that, Shiina, 
why don't we all play a new game instead?</b>

07:18.960 --> 07:20.080
<b>Huh?</b>

07:20.300 --> 07:24.590
<b>You understand what I just said, right?
 If we play this out, we all lose.</b>

07:24.980 --> 07:28.090
<b>Well, I, um, <i>guess</i> you're right there?</b>

07:28.910 --> 07:32.430
<b>So, let's make it more black and white,
 and get a <i>real</i> winner instead.</b>

07:32.430 --> 07:34.090
<b>We'll play a game called Crossboard.</b>

07:34.740 --> 07:37.980
<b>It's a turn-based board game 
that works inside ASTRAL.</b>

07:37.980 --> 07:42.840
<b>If you can beat me at it, you'll win 
the battle for the title of Empress, too.</b>

07:42.840 --> 07:45.870
<b>It also gives us a fighting chance.</b>

07:46.870 --> 07:48.350
<b>I'm on board with that.</b>

07:51.420 --> 07:54.270
<b>Come on, Shiina. 
Can you really turn this down?</b>

07:55.670 --> 07:59.920
<b>This is an invitation to the exact kind of 
star-catching game you always wanted to play.</b>

07:59.920 --> 08:02.970
<b>And your opponents are 
a Six Star genius princess,</b>

08:03.930 --> 08:06.170
<b>and the fastest guy to reach Seven Stars.</b>

08:06.590 --> 08:10.000
<b>If you pass this up now, I doubt 
you'll get a chance like it again.</b>

08:10.000 --> 08:11.620
<b>Ah, you're right!</b>

08:11.620 --> 08:13.210
<b>Okay, then, bro-bro.</b>

08:13.740 --> 08:17.620
<b>Let's finish this with 
a game of Crossboard.</b>

08:20.300 --> 08:22.460
<b>Wow!</b>

08:23.590 --> 08:25.890
<b>Oh, boy! Oh, boy!</b>

08:29.900 --> 08:31.650
<b>I can see everything.</b>

08:31.650 --> 08:34.190
<b>What a huge production.</b>

08:34.190 --> 08:35.980
<b>This is pretty crazy.</b>

08:39.990 --> 08:43.000
<b>Crossboard</b>

08:43.310 --> 08:47.500
<b>In Crossboard, all the ASTRAL spaces 
get compressed into just 100 spaces.</b>

08:47.960 --> 08:50.500
<b>Positions and abilities 
are all carried over.</b>

08:50.850 --> 08:54.500
<b>If you lose all of your spaces or 
your core base, you lose the game.</b>

08:56.010 --> 09:01.540
<b>And this bit's really important. 
Crossboard is fully integrated with ASTRAL.</b>

09:01.540 --> 09:06.350
<b>Every change on this game board 
will be reflected on the ASTRAL field.</b>

09:06.350 --> 09:11.040
<b>So whoever destroys all of Eimei's
 spaces first will be the real Empress.</b>

09:11.040 --> 09:14.680
<b>Oh, wow. I'll start then, okay?</b>

09:14.680 --> 09:16.160
<b><i>It is Shiina Tsumugi's turn.</i></b>

09:16.610 --> 09:16.660
<b>Encroach</b>

09:16.610 --> 09:16.660
<b>Conquer</b>

09:16.650 --> 09:18.270
<b>First, take a main action.</b>

09:16.660 --> 09:16.700
<b>Encroach</b>

09:16.660 --> 09:16.700
<b>Conquer</b>

09:16.700 --> 09:18.280
<b>Encroach</b>

09:16.700 --> 09:18.280
<b>Conquer</b>

09:18.280 --> 09:19.240
<b>Encroach</b>

09:18.280 --> 09:19.240
<b>Conquer</b>

09:19.240 --> 09:22.750
<b>Encroach</b>

09:19.240 --> 09:22.750
<b>Conquer</b>

09:19.250 --> 09:22.750
<b>There are two types of flags. 
Select one and place it on the board.</b>

09:23.040 --> 09:26.030
<b>You can only put it on a space 
adjacent to an area you hold.</b>

09:25.620 --> 09:27.250
<b>Conquer Flag</b>

09:25.620 --> 09:27.250
<b>Immediately turns selected space to your own team's color</b>

09:25.620 --> 09:27.250
<b>Encroach Flag</b>

09:25.620 --> 09:27.250
<b>When the next turn ends, 
attached spaces turn to your own team's color</b>

09:26.030 --> 09:27.250
<b>Uh-huh.</b>

09:27.250 --> 09:27.420
<b>Encroach</b>

09:27.250 --> 09:27.420
<b>Conquer</b>

09:27.420 --> 09:27.460
<b>Encroach</b>

09:27.420 --> 09:27.460
<b>Conquer</b>

09:27.460 --> 09:27.500
<b>Encroach</b>

09:27.460 --> 09:27.500
<b>Conquer</b>

09:28.800 --> 09:30.340
<b>Okay, I picked!</b>

09:32.360 --> 09:35.520
<b>Aw, I guess that wasn't your core base.</b>

09:35.520 --> 09:37.750
<b>You thought you'd win on the first turn?</b>

09:38.010 --> 09:43.020
<b>Collect</b>

09:38.010 --> 09:43.020
<b>Move</b>

09:38.010 --> 09:43.020
<b>Disrupt</b>

09:38.050 --> 09:43.020
<b>Collect Information: Select a space in the enemy's area to determine if it is the core base or not</b>

09:38.180 --> 09:39.920
<b>Next is the sub-action.</b>

09:39.300 --> 09:43.020
<b>Move: Move your own team's core base up to two spaces from its current spot</b>

09:39.920 --> 09:42.610
<b>There are three, and you 
can choose to activate one.</b>

09:40.550 --> 09:43.020
<b>Disrupt: For one turn, disable all information collection about your team</b>

09:43.010 --> 09:45.010
<b>What will I pick?</b>

09:43.020 --> 09:45.020
<b>Disrupt</b>

09:43.020 --> 09:45.020
<b>Collect</b>

09:43.020 --> 09:45.020
<b>Move</b>

09:45.010 --> 09:48.020
<b>Okay, I'll try it on a space Empress owns.</b>

09:48.500 --> 09:50.680
<b>Aw, I missed.</b>

09:50.680 --> 09:52.910
<b>All right, it's your turn now, bro-bro!</b>

09:52.910 --> 09:54.730
<b><i>It is Shinohara Hiroto's turn.</i></b>

09:55.020 --> 09:56.020
<b>Right.</b>

09:55.490 --> 09:55.540
<b>Encroach</b>

09:55.490 --> 09:55.540
<b>Conquer</b>

09:55.540 --> 09:55.580
<b>Encroach</b>

09:55.540 --> 09:55.580
<b>Conquer</b>

09:55.580 --> 09:56.530
<b>Encroach</b>

09:55.580 --> 09:56.530
<b>Conquer</b>

09:56.530 --> 09:58.490
<b>Encroach</b>

09:56.530 --> 09:58.490
<b>Conquer</b>

09:58.490 --> 09:59.550
<b>Huh?</b>

09:59.550 --> 10:01.980
<b>Huh?! Are you crazy, bro-bro?</b>

10:02.360 --> 10:05.980
<b>You've only got two spaces left,
and you aren't taking one right away?</b>

10:05.980 --> 10:09.790
<b>Are you trying to let me 
win out of brotherly love?</b>

10:09.790 --> 10:13.060
<b>Not a chance. I'm not 
your brother to begin with.</b>

10:13.380 --> 10:16.470
<b>Disrupt</b>

10:13.980 --> 10:16.610
<b>Then, I'll use Disrupt as my sub-action.</b>

10:16.470 --> 10:16.510
<b>Disrupt</b>

10:16.510 --> 10:16.550
<b>Disrupt</b>

10:16.960 --> 10:18.480
<b>We're done for.</b>

10:18.920 --> 10:21.470
<b>Huh? What do you mean by that?</b>

10:21.790 --> 10:26.770
<b>Can't you see? Neither of us 
can attack Eimei anymore.</b>

10:26.770 --> 10:31.690
<b>Eimei has two spaces left, 
but we don't know which one is the core,</b>

10:31.690 --> 10:35.980
<b>and after my turn, Seijo can place a flag.
 You know what that means?</b>

10:36.330 --> 10:37.480
<b>Oh!</b>

10:37.740 --> 10:39.130
<b>Yup, right.</b>

10:39.130 --> 10:44.420
<b>You both want to beat me, of course, 
but since Crossboard is turn-based,</b>

10:44.420 --> 10:49.210
<b>if you get Eimei down to one space, 
the other team will definitely win.</b>

10:50.950 --> 10:54.470
<b>In other words, neither of you can attack me.</b>

10:54.470 --> 10:57.080
<b>In fact, you have to <i>protect</i> me
 from the other person.</b>

10:57.080 --> 11:00.720
<b>D-Did you plan this 
from the start, bro-bro?</b>

11:01.020 --> 11:02.550
<b>Of course I did.</b>

11:05.460 --> 11:08.610
<b>Well, it doesn't really matter for Ouka.</b>

11:08.610 --> 11:10.350
<b><i>It is Saionji Sarasa's turn.</i></b>

11:09.180 --> 11:09.230
<b>Encroach</b>

11:09.180 --> 11:09.230
<b>Conquer</b>

11:09.230 --> 11:09.270
<b>Encroach</b>

11:09.230 --> 11:09.270
<b>Conquer</b>

11:09.270 --> 11:10.730
<b>Encroach</b>

11:09.270 --> 11:10.730
<b>Conquer</b>

11:14.210 --> 11:16.270
<b>And Disrupt as my sub-action.</b>

11:16.270 --> 11:18.070
<b><i>It is Shiina Tsumugi's turn.</i></b>

11:16.270 --> 11:21.280
<b>Encroach</b>

11:16.270 --> 11:21.280
<b>Conquer</b>

11:18.070 --> 11:21.270
<b>Um, um, um, um... What should I do?</b>

11:21.590 --> 11:27.720
<b><i>It really looks like Shiina plays to enjoy the
 game and isn't the type to cheat just to win.</i></b>

11:27.720 --> 11:31.630
<b>Hey! What's going on? How come 
Ouka's spaces are being taken?</b>

11:32.280 --> 11:35.290
<b>Huh? Why's the color changing like that?</b>

11:35.540 --> 11:37.660
<b>It isn't one of your abilities?</b>

11:37.660 --> 11:41.180
<b>Huh? Hm, I don't know.</b>

11:41.170 --> 11:46.680
<b>Encroach</b>

11:41.170 --> 11:46.680
<b>Conquer</b>

11:41.510 --> 11:46.690
<b>Ah! Maybe my evil powers are so strong,
they've taken the board to the dark side.</b>

11:46.690 --> 11:49.240
<b>Uh, sure. That's definitely it.</b>

11:50.070 --> 11:52.970
<b><i>But Shiina hasn't taken an action yet.</i></b>

11:52.970 --> 11:55.180
<b><i>There's only one explanation I can think of.</i></b>

11:55.360 --> 11:56.440
<b>Crossboard</b>

11:56.430 --> 11:57.950
<b>Wh-What's going on?</b>

12:04.460 --> 12:06.700
<b><i>They're not the real deal,
 just corrupt copies.</i></b>

12:07.210 --> 12:09.460
<b>They're probably like Miss Hundred Faces.</b>

12:09.460 --> 12:11.210
<b>Huh? Just like me?</b>

12:11.210 --> 12:15.170
<b>The same tech that copied those 
players' likenesses. Is that what you mean?</b>

12:15.640 --> 12:19.840
<b>Yeah. He's using them 
to expand his area by force.</b>

12:20.530 --> 12:24.360
<b>Oh! Yeah, that's it, bro-bro!</b>

12:24.360 --> 12:25.800
<b>Aren't I a genius?</b>

12:26.210 --> 12:30.160
<b><i>Kurahashi must be the one 
making these corrupt copies appear.</i></b>

12:30.160 --> 12:33.780
<b><i>Damn it. He's just gonna
shamelessly force a win for himself.</i></b>

12:33.780 --> 12:36.980
<b>Okay. I'm starting to feel like I can win.</b>

12:40.930 --> 12:44.240
<b><i>If I lose one more space, I'm done for.</i></b>

12:44.240 --> 12:45.250
<b>Shinohara?</b>

12:45.250 --> 12:49.910
<b>Since the two games are connected, 
it wouldn't be hard to manipulate this one, too.</b>

12:49.910 --> 12:52.260
<b>But then, why make that kind of rule?</b>

12:52.740 --> 12:54.210
<b>That's obvious.</b>

12:54.650 --> 12:58.080
<b>The returns are way bigger than the risks.</b>

12:58.080 --> 13:01.980
<b>And my teammates are the strongest around.</b>

13:01.980 --> 13:03.740
<b><i>It is Shinohara Hiroto's turn.</i></b>

13:10.150 --> 13:12.750
<b>Nanase! On your left and right!</b>

13:12.750 --> 13:15.590
<b>Jump by kicking off with 
your strong leg, then fire right!</b>

13:15.590 --> 13:19.770
<b>Block left using Barrier, back away,
 then spam Magic Blast!</b>

13:20.170 --> 13:22.100
<b><i>Too many orders!</i></b>

13:26.770 --> 13:28.340
<b>There. Owned.</b>

13:28.930 --> 13:30.250
<b><i>See? Told you.</i></b>

13:30.910 --> 13:33.830
<b><i>You need to quit grumbling 
and just do what I say.</i></b>

13:33.830 --> 13:37.200
<b>H-Huh? Can't you even
 give me <i>one</i> compliment?</b>

13:37.200 --> 13:40.790
<b>Do you think I'm your lapdog or something?</b>

13:41.580 --> 13:43.870
<b><i>Of course. That goes without saying.</i></b>

13:43.870 --> 13:49.420
<b><i>Only one person follows my instructions to 
the letter, and that's you, Asamiya Nanase.</i></b>

13:50.390 --> 13:56.230
<b>Y-You dummy. You make it sound 
like I have total faith in you.</b>

13:56.600 --> 13:57.730
<b><i>Am I wrong in that?</i></b>

13:58.020 --> 14:00.370
<b><i>D-Don't sound so down about it.</i></b>

14:00.370 --> 14:04.110
<b><i>If I didn't trust you, 
I wouldn't let you watch my back.</i></b>

14:04.490 --> 14:05.630
<b>Is that right?</b>

14:06.510 --> 14:10.990
<b>But, Nanase, is it <i>really</i> accurate 
to say I'm watching your back</b>

14:10.990 --> 14:13.750
<b>when I'm barking instructions 
from a safe spot far away?</b>

14:13.750 --> 14:17.510
<b><i>Jeez. Don't be so literal, Shinji, you idiot!</i></b>

14:17.510 --> 14:20.700
<b>Asamiya Nanase and Enomoto Shinji?</b>

14:21.740 --> 14:23.470
<b>How are they still alive?</b>

14:23.870 --> 14:26.430
<b>Kirigaya was supposed 
to have taken them out.</b>

14:32.480 --> 14:34.160
<b>Lightning Rod?</b>

14:35.180 --> 14:40.730
<b>Damn it! Even the server logs have 
been falsified! Libra must be in on it!</b>

14:41.970 --> 14:47.340
<b>This was all part of your plan, 
wasn't it, Shinohara Hiroto?</b>

14:52.490 --> 14:55.990
<b>Ah, I guess I always go back to the same plan.</b>

14:55.990 --> 15:01.100
<b>If I send in a different player, 
I can take control of ASTRAL again.</b>

15:01.640 --> 15:06.000
<b>I hired this guy exactly for that purpose.</b>

15:09.110 --> 15:14.380
<b><i>It's time, Kirigaya. Go and show them
 just how powerful we are.</i></b>

15:14.730 --> 15:18.070
<b>Nah, ain't gonna happen.</b>

15:18.070 --> 15:19.220
<b>What?</b>

15:20.130 --> 15:24.860
<b>Kurahashi, Shinohara can already 
see through your crappy plan.</b>

15:24.860 --> 15:28.360
<b>I'm not some idiot who's gonna play
 a game I know I can't win.</b>

15:28.360 --> 15:30.030
<b><i>What are you talking about?</i></b>

15:30.030 --> 15:33.070
<b>You're my pawn! You do what I say—</b>

15:33.070 --> 15:35.570
<b>You're totally worthless to me.</b>

15:37.070 --> 15:41.780
<b>Someone like you could 
never take on a Seven Star.</b>

15:41.780 --> 15:45.580
<b>You're finished, Kurahashi Mikado.</b>

15:49.970 --> 15:53.470
<b>Damn it! You damn punks!</b>

15:54.600 --> 15:58.140
<b>Turn five. The situation's 
changed quite a bit.</b>

15:58.470 --> 16:00.050
<b><i>It is Shiina Tsumugi's turn.</i></b>

16:01.930 --> 16:04.480
<b>You're too tough on me, bro-bro.</b>

16:04.720 --> 16:07.520
<b>That's because I can't afford to lose.</b>

16:07.520 --> 16:13.480
<b><i>But man, Saionji's keeping up without
 cheating at all. That blows my mind.</i></b>

16:13.480 --> 16:16.600
<b>Huh? I feel kinda weird.</b>

16:16.600 --> 16:18.490
<b>Weird? What do you mean?</b>

16:18.490 --> 16:25.040
<b>Like my body isn't doing what I tell it. 
I can't move right.</b>

16:27.590 --> 16:30.800
<b>What? What? If I touch it, 
it becomes my area?</b>

16:33.900 --> 16:38.230
<b><i>It must be Kurahashi. 
He's finally taken full control of Shiina.</i></b>

16:38.230 --> 16:41.510
<b>Seriously. That guy's 
the worst kind of loser.</b>

16:41.510 --> 16:45.050
<b>Well, at least this gives us
 everything we need.</b>

16:45.750 --> 16:47.770
<b><i>It is Shinohara Hiroto's turn.</i></b>

16:47.770 --> 16:50.650
<b>Ability Tracing, activate.</b>

16:50.650 --> 16:54.270
<b><i>Yo, Kurahashi. You hearing me?</i></b>

16:55.770 --> 17:00.660
<b><i>I've won it all this time. 
Surrender like a good boy.</i></b>

17:01.540 --> 17:02.870
<b><i>Damn.</i></b>

17:02.870 --> 17:08.080
<b><i>Oh. Yeah, yeah. About this 
Ability Tracing I'm using right now...</i></b>

17:08.080 --> 17:11.910
<b><i>It does just what it says and 
shows me exactly where you are.</i></b>

17:11.910 --> 17:16.090
<b>So what? That won't help you 
while you're still inside ASTRAL!</b>

17:16.090 --> 17:21.280
<b><i>Sure it will. Eimei has four 
other players besides me.</i></b>

17:21.800 --> 17:25.230
<b><i>You've seen what Asamiya 
and Enomoto are doing,</i></b>

17:25.230 --> 17:29.500
<b><i>but where are the other two? 
I wonder what could they be up to.</i></b>

17:36.450 --> 17:37.940
<b>Y-You are...</b>

17:37.940 --> 17:42.340
<b>Shinohara Hiroto-sama's 
personal maid, Himeji Shirayuki.</b>

17:43.400 --> 17:48.890
<b>I've been told you have a new game here 
that lets you control Miss Hundred Faces.</b>

17:49.400 --> 17:51.890
<b>You're just one girl. 
What can you do about it?</b>

17:51.890 --> 17:54.990
<b>Just one girl? Don't be silly.</b>

17:54.990 --> 17:58.750
<b>I've never been good 
with the opposite sex...</b>

18:02.830 --> 18:05.110
<b>So she brought all of us along.</b>

18:05.110 --> 18:06.930
<b>Why the hell are you all here?!</b>

18:08.280 --> 18:10.220
<b>Do you still intend to persist?</b>

18:14.460 --> 18:18.250
<b><i>After Himeji and the others 
broke into Kurahashi's base,</i></b>

18:18.730 --> 18:20.710
<b><i>things wrapped up quickly.</i></b>

18:22.510 --> 18:25.240
<b><i>Himeji took control of Miss Hundred Faces,</i></b>

18:25.630 --> 18:28.070
<b><i>and turned the board green.</i></b>

18:28.070 --> 18:34.570
<b><i>As a result, the Seijo area and all the power
 it held disappeared completely.</i></b>

18:35.320 --> 18:37.620
<b><i>Shiina Tsumugi, you have been eliminated.</i></b>

18:40.840 --> 18:44.790
<b>Is it over? Is it all over now?</b>

18:44.790 --> 18:47.670
<b>Yep. You lost, Shiina.</b>

18:47.670 --> 18:50.650
<b>I guess you just picked the 
wrong opponents this time.</b>

18:50.650 --> 18:54.300
<b>Hm, I guess. Yeah, you might be right.</b>

18:54.300 --> 18:59.240
<b>Yeah. I lost in ASTRAL. 
I'm okay with that part.</b>

18:59.660 --> 19:05.160
<b>But... was I really doing something bad?</b>

19:05.160 --> 19:06.540
<b>Shiina...</b>

19:07.280 --> 19:11.040
<b><i>No, I'm not the right person 
to answer that question.</i></b>

19:16.470 --> 19:17.490
<b>Kazami?</b>

19:18.010 --> 19:20.660
<b>Shinohara-kun. Sarasa-chan.</b>

19:21.010 --> 19:23.200
<b>There's one thing I need to ask.</b>

19:24.370 --> 19:28.680
<b>How do you and Libra feel 
about Shiina Tsumugi right now?</b>

19:29.330 --> 19:30.530
<b>Tsumugi-chan.</b>

19:30.530 --> 19:31.470
<b>Huh?</b>

19:32.120 --> 19:33.730
<b>Will you tell me something, meow?</b>

19:36.060 --> 19:38.570
<b>How was ASTRAL for you, meow?</b>

19:38.570 --> 19:39.160
<b>Huh?</b>

19:39.470 --> 19:41.670
<b>Was it really boring, meow?</b>

19:41.670 --> 19:45.170
<b>No, it wasn't. It wasn't boring at all!</b>

19:45.470 --> 19:48.370
<b>It was really, really fun.</b>

19:48.370 --> 19:53.160
<b>ASTRAL and MTCG and even Crossboard...
 It was all really fun!</b>

19:53.520 --> 19:55.960
<b>I'm so sad it's over.</b>

19:55.960 --> 20:00.670
<b>I wish I could've kept playing forever 
and ever! It was so much fun!</b>

20:01.300 --> 20:03.390
<b>I'm relieved to hear that, meow.</b>

20:03.390 --> 20:08.580
<b>We really did our best to 
make it fun for everyone, meow.</b>

20:09.180 --> 20:14.570
<b>And things really did take off when that 
super enemy, Miss Hundred Faces, appeared.</b>

20:14.570 --> 20:18.990
<b>So if you're saying you had fun, 
that makes me super, super happy.</b>

20:18.990 --> 20:20.590
<b>It's 10 out of 10 for you, meow!</b>

20:20.590 --> 20:22.170
<b>Wow, 10 out of 10!</b>

20:22.170 --> 20:25.580
<b>Oh, I'm so glad.</b>

20:30.530 --> 20:32.940
<b><i>I guess things are gonna be all right.</i></b>

20:33.850 --> 20:38.410
<b><i>Eimei takes the win in 
both Crossroad and ASTRAL.</i></b>

20:38.790 --> 20:42.600
<b>Wait, what? Why isn't 
the ASTRAL field clearing?</b>

20:43.480 --> 20:44.420
<b><i>How come?</i></b>

20:44.430 --> 20:45.180
<b>Map</b>

20:44.430 --> 20:45.180
<b>District 4's 
Eimei Academy</b>

20:47.850 --> 20:51.430
<b>I managed to save Ouka's core base.</b>

20:51.740 --> 20:57.440
<b>You wanted to win <i>and</i> take every last space?
 I won't let you show off like that.</b>

20:59.200 --> 21:00.330
<b>Of course.</b>

21:06.260 --> 21:08.020
<b>Hiroto-kun!</b>

21:08.020 --> 21:09.800
<b>Shino, good work!</b>

21:09.800 --> 21:10.950
<b>Very well played.</b>

21:11.210 --> 21:13.670
<b>Welcome back, Master.</b>

21:13.670 --> 21:15.440
<b>Yeah. Glad to be back.</b>

21:15.440 --> 21:18.340
<b>You turned it all around right at the end.</b>

21:18.340 --> 21:20.960
<b>I think I've fallen for you even harder!</b>

21:20.960 --> 21:22.590
<b>Not so close, Akizuki-sama.</b>

21:22.590 --> 21:25.370
<b>Huh? I haven't even touched him yet.</b>

21:28.140 --> 21:32.260
<b>In all honesty, your results this time
wildly exceeded my expectations.</b>

21:32.260 --> 21:35.010
<b>As student council president, 
I owe you my thanks.</b>

21:35.010 --> 21:38.220
<b>Well, <i>obviously</i>! You haven't 
been paying attention, Shinji.</b>

21:38.490 --> 21:41.740
<b>Nah. It was all thanks to you guys.</b>

21:42.110 --> 21:46.400
<b>Oh, was it now? In that case, 
I retract my words of gratitude.</b>

21:46.750 --> 21:48.660
<b>That retraction sure came quick.</b>

21:48.660 --> 21:50.500
<b>You still weren't polite enough.</b>

22:03.260 --> 22:04.490
<b><i>Everything began...</i></b>

22:06.030 --> 22:08.230
<b><i>with a single lie.</i></b>

22:11.930 --> 22:13.550
<b><i>A single lie...</i></b>

22:14.730 --> 22:16.290
<b><i>can save someone.</i></b>

22:20.160 --> 22:21.720
<b><i>A single lie...</i></b>

22:22.800 --> 22:24.750
<b><i>can gain you many new friends.</i></b>

22:27.700 --> 22:29.950
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

22:27.700 --> 22:29.950
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

22:27.700 --> 22:29.950
<b>Seijo Academy eliminated due to disqualification</b>

22:28.550 --> 22:29.940
<b><i>A single lie...</i></b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>May Inter-Academy Battle "ASTRAL" Final Results</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>1st Place</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>Eimei Academy</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>2nd Place</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>Ouka Academy</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>3rd Place</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>Tsuyuri Girls'
 Academy</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>4th Place</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>Otowa Academy</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>5th Place</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>Shinra Academy</b>

22:29.950 --> 22:32.240
<b>Seijo Academy eliminated due to disqualification</b>

22:32.250 --> 22:34.510
<b><i>can change your whole life.</i></b>

22:44.770 --> 22:46.160
<b><i>But now, this lie...</i></b>

22:47.910 --> 22:50.390
<b><i>doesn't just belong to me.</i></b>

22:51.930 --> 22:53.290
<b>Hello, Master.</b>

22:53.580 --> 22:59.580
<b><i>Someday, somewhere on Academy Island, 
I'll find the one I'm searching for.</i></b>

23:00.070 --> 23:01.330
<b><i>And until that day...</i></b>

23:08.590 --> 23:10.430
<b>He's here! The Seven Star!</b>

23:09.710 --> 23:11.400
<b>The strongest on Academy Island!</b>

23:11.400 --> 23:13.690
<b>How's he gonna fight this time?</b>

23:13.690 --> 23:15.040
<b>I can't wait to find out.</b>

23:24.650 --> 23:25.640
<b>Ready?</b>

23:26.420 --> 23:28.460
<b>The game's about to start.</b>

23:28.460 --> 23:31.500
<b><i>Together with my friends here,</i></b>

23:31.500 --> 23:34.280
<b><i>I'm gonna keep on lying.</i></b>
